	{ version = "1.5.5-beta.3", date = "2026-11-26", blocks = {
		{ "h", "Changed: the settings window is easy to drive with the D-pad" },
		{ "b", "The D-pad now moves freely up, down, left and right on every tab. No more dead ends: in Tweaks you can cross the columns from any row, and in Rings you can go from the settings up to the ring and left to the ring list.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Choices are real dropdowns,|r like the game's own settings. No more left/right arrows: press |cffffd200A|r (or click) on a choice and a list opens under it. Up and down move, |cffffd200A|r picks, |cffffd200B|r closes. The current option is gold. Rumble patterns play once when you pick one, and |cffffd200Y|r tests them.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Sliders:|r press |cffffd200A|r to grab one, then left and right change it. |cffffd200A|r or |cffffd200B|r lets go, and up or down lets go and moves on.", 1 },
		{ "b", "In Bindings, |cffffd200Page n of 3|r opens a page list; L2 and R2 still flip pages.", 1 },
		{ "h", "New: rings take the mouse" },
		{ "b", "Like the game's own radial flyout: move the mouse over a ring's slot and it lights up with its tooltip (the party member on a healer ring). Click it to use it, right click to close the ring. Works on Hold, Toggle and healer rings, in combat too.", 1 },
		{ "b", "On a Hold ring, letting go of the button with the stick centred uses the slot under the mouse. A pushed stick still wins.", 1 },
		{ "h", "New: the logo in the window's corner" },
		{ "b", "The Controller Tweaks window wears the round logo in its top-left corner, in the game's gold portrait ring. |cffffd200Restart the game once|r (not just /reload) so the new picture loads.", 1 },
	} },
	{ version = "1.5.5-beta.2", date = "2026-11-26", blocks = {
		{ "h", "Fixed: the other stick feels native while a ring is open" },
		{ "b", "Beta.1's fix moved you with keys instead of the stick: opening a ring cancelled your run, the camera stayed locked while you turned, and the right stick turned your character in place instead of the camera.", 1 },
		{ "b", "Now the stick you don't aim with is the game's own stick again. A ring on the right stick: the left stick walks and runs as usual, and the camera follows. A ring on the left stick: the right stick moves the camera as usual. Only the aiming stick is kept from the game, and after you let go it stays kept until it's back in the middle, so you don't walk off or swing the camera. Works in combat.", 1 },
		{ "b", "The |cffffd200Ring open: left stick moves|r and |cffffd200Ring open: right stick turns|r settings are gone: there's nothing to turn off any more.", 1 },
		{ "h", "New: different rings and actions on each crossbar page" },
		{ "b", "A button's ring or action now belongs to the crossbar page you set it on, so page 1, 2 and 3 can each have their own. Switch pages in Bindings with |cffffd200L2 / R2|r and set each one.", 1 },
		{ "b", "Your current setup is copied to all three pages, so nothing changes until you edit a page. The back paddles, L3 / R3 and the Jump, Back, Interact and Inspect spots stay the same on every page.", 1 },
		{ "h", "Fixed: forms and stances, again" },
		{ "b", "A macro or ring on the stance bar's layer still didn't fire in some forms. The press now asks the game which form bar is up at that moment, so it works in Stealth, Cat and Bear Form and stances.", 1 },
		{ "b", "/fct status shows a form line (what the addon sees for your form). If a form still misbehaves, send us that line.", 1 },
		{ "h", "Fixed: Best healing potion and Best mana potion" },
		{ "b", "They did nothing when the potions weren't loaded yet after login, or when the game filed a potion under another kind of item. They now find them, and say so when you have none.", 1 },
		{ "h", "New: Options → AddOns page" },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Forever Controller Tweaks|r is listed under Options → AddOns, with a button that opens the addon's window. The controller can't reach that page's button (the game only lets it move through setting rows); use the mouse or touch, or the usual shortcut.", 1 },
		{ "h", "Changed: your bindings stay on the crossbar while the window is open" },
		{ "b", "With Bindings (or any of the addon's tabs) open, the crossbar used to show the game's own face actions, so it looked as if your bindings were gone. It now keeps showing your bindings, on the page shown, and updates as you edit. Your buttons still drive the window and cast nothing while it's open.", 1 },
		{ "h", "Fixed: keyboard Shift and Symbols moved around" },
		{ "b", "Depending on your modifier setup, Shift and Symbols on the on-screen keyboard jumped between L1, L2 and R1. They're now always the physical triggers: |cffffd200L2|r is Shift, |cffffd200R2|r is Symbols, both together the extra symbols. L1 does nothing on the keyboard.", 1 },
		{ "h", "Sync" },
		{ "b", "Sync is written in a new format that carries the per-page bindings. A computer still on 1.5.4 or older pauses sync and says to update; it never writes over the newer copy.", 1 },
	} },
	{ version = "1.5.5-beta.1", date = "2026-11-25", blocks = {
		{ "h", "Fixed: a ring stopped your movement" },
		{ "b", "While a held ring was open, the stick you don't aim with did nothing: you stopped running (unless Auto Run was on), or the camera froze. The game's stick-as-buttons setting that rings need covers both sticks.", 1 },
		{ "b", "Now that stick keeps working. A ring that aims with the right stick: the |cffffd200left stick moves you|r, full speed in 8 directions. A ring that aims with the left stick: the |cffffd200right stick turns and tilts the camera|r, at a fixed speed. The ring still aims and fires as before. Healer rings too; touch rings don't change.", 1 },
		{ "b", "Close the ring while still running and you keep running until you let the stick go; you never keep running after that.", 1 },
		{ "b", "After a ring is used in combat, both sticks keep working this way until the fight ends: the left stick moves you (8 directions, full speed) and the right stick turns the camera (a fixed speed). After the fight they are analog again.", 1 },
		{ "b", "Each stick has its own setting in Tweaks → Controller: |cffffd200Ring open: left stick moves|r and |cffffd200Ring open: right stick turns|r. Both are on; turn one off to get the old behaviour for that stick.", 1 },
		{ "h", "Fixed: a shapeshift form cast the normal bar's spell" },
		{ "b", "In a form that swaps a bar (a Druid's Cat or Bear Form, a Rogue's Stealth, a Warrior's stances), a face button with a ring or another action on that bar's layer sometimes cast the normal bar's spell instead of the form's, which knocked a Druid out of form. Rebinding a spell only fixed it for a while.", 1 },
		{ "b", "The button now follows the game's own rule: while the form's bar is up and you are on its page, the press goes to the form's bar, even in the instant after you shift or while the bar isn't drawn yet. On other pages, and out of form, it goes to your normal bar or your ring as before.", 1 },
	} },
	{ version = "1.5.4", date = "2026-11-21", blocks = {
		{ "h", "Changed: profiles belong to the character, controllers don't matter" },
		{ "b", "The game reports one controller under several names (Steam Link, Android, the pad itself), and 1.5.1 picked a profile per name, so a character could land on a profile without its bindings: \"the bars are gone\". Now each character has its own profiles and plays on one of them, whichever controller you use. Plugging in another pad, or the same pad seen differently, never changes your bindings, touch buttons or layout.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Profiles are per character:|r the Settings tab, |cffffd200New profile|r, |cffffd200Copy profile|r, |cffffd200Delete profile|r and /fct profile show and change this character's profiles only. Want a different setup? Make a new profile and switch to it.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200No more new-controller question.|r The Settings tab's Controllers list is gone too.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200After the update|r each character keeps the profile its bindings were on (the one you used last, else the one with the most bindings), with every binding and touch button. Older settings waiting for their character take their profile along when the character claims them.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200A new character|r starts on |cffffd200Default|r with the layout of the character you played last on this computer, and no bindings.", 1 },
		{ "h", "Fixed: battery icon under the minimap ring" },
		{ "b", "The controller battery on the minimap sat partly under the minimap's ring. It now draws over the ring, on the same circle as the game's own round button.", 1 },
		{ "h", "Sync" },
		{ "b", "Sync is written in a new format that carries each character's profiles. A computer still on 1.5.3 or older pauses sync and says to update; it never writes over the newer copy. Update the addon on every computer you sync.", 1 },
		{ "b", "Sets written by older versions still read: their bindings come in, their account-wide profiles and controller picks don't.", 1 },
	} },
	{ version = "1.5.3", date = "2026-11-21", blocks = {
		{ "h", "Fixed: error with a pet" },
		{ "b", "Opening the action picker (choosing an action for a button) on a character with a pet, such as a Warlock with an Imp, showed a Lua error and the picker stayed closed. The pet's spells now list normally.", 1 },
		{ "h", "Fixed: Learn all never showed on the trainer" },
		{ "b", "With the Gamepad UI on, the game hides the trainer's own Train button, and |cffffd200Learn all|r (Tweaks → Trainer: Learn all) only showed while that button did. It now shows whenever the trainer window is open.", 1 },
	} },
	{ version = "1.5.2", date = "2026-11-21", blocks = {
		{ "h", "Fixed: a new character got another character's bindings" },
		{ "b", "WoW: Forever characters have a first and a second name, and the game tells addons only the first. 1.5.1 saved settings under that first name, so every character with the same first name shared them: a new character could start with another one's bindings, touch buttons and rings.", 1 },
		{ "b", "Settings are now saved per character by its unique game ID. After the update, the old settings go back to the character they belong to: the one that knows every spell in them takes them, newest first. Settings no character can be sure of are kept as they are, untouched. A new character starts empty: no bindings, no touch buttons, no rings.", 1 },
		{ "h", "Changed: rings are per character" },
		{ "b", "Each character has its own rings. After the update, each character's old settings keep the rings their buttons open, and rings no button opens go along with all of them. A new character starts without rings, even if it is the first you log in with after the update.", 1 },
		{ "b", "The Rings tab, the picker and /fct rings show this character's rings. Deleting a ring clears only this character's buttons that open it. |cffffd200Arrow on ring buttons|r stays one setting for all characters.", 1 },
		{ "h", "Changed: touch buttons are per profile" },
		{ "b", "What each touch button does is now saved per profile, like bindings: a new profile starts with empty touch buttons, |cffffd200Copy profile|r copies them, and |cffffd200Delete profile|r deletes them. The touch bars' size, place, shape and On / Show stay one setting per character.", 1 },
		{ "b", "After the update every profile you have keeps the touch buttons you had.", 1 },
		{ "h", "New: zoom the camera" },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Zoom in|r and |cffffd200Zoom out|r in the picker's |cffffd200Misc|r category: a press moves the camera one step, holding keeps it moving until you let go. They work in combat too. On a touch button or ring slot a tap is one step.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Tweaks → Camera → Camera zoom:|r where the camera sits, in yards, up to the game's own limit. Moving it zooms at once, and the camera goes back there when you log in. Untouched, the addon never moves your camera.", 1 },
		{ "h", "Sync" },
		{ "b", "Sync is written in a new format. A computer still on 1.5.1 pauses sync and says to update; it never writes over the newer copy. Update the addon on every computer you sync.", 1 },
		{ "b", "Rings sync per character and touch buttons per profile. The first time two computers meet after the update, a character keeps every ring either computer gave it. An export from 1.5.1 still imports: its rings go to this character, its touch buttons to this controller's profile.", 1 },
	} },
	{ version = "1.5.1", date = "2026-11-21", blocks = {
		{ "h", "New: profiles, share bindings between controllers" },
		{ "b", "Your layout (which buttons are modifiers, where Jump and Interact sit) and every character's bindings now live in a |cffffd200profile|r. Controllers on the same profile share all of it: bind a spell on your DualSense and it is on your GameSir too. Glyphs and button setup still follow each physical controller.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Nothing changes for you after the update:|r each controller you already used becomes its own profile, named after it, with its layout and bindings as they were. Share one when you choose to.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200A new controller asks once:|r |cffffd200Use|r a profile you have (shared, the same bindings), |cffffd200Copy|r one into a new profile to change on its own, or start |cffffd200New empty|r (the game's layout, no bindings). With more than one profile, a stepper picks which one Use and Copy act on. Until you answer, the new controller plays on the profile you used last; |cffffd200Circle|r answers Use. The question waits for the end of a fight, a loading screen, the controller setup and the setup guide.", 1 },
		{ "b", "Your very first controller gets a |cffffd200Default|r profile without asking.", 1 },
		{ "b", "/fct profile lists your profiles; /fct profile <name> switches this controller to one.", 1 },
		{ "h", "New: Settings tab" },
		{ "b", "A sixth side tab after Tweaks, in the same look:", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Profile:|r the profile this controller uses (left/right switches it, out of combat), its |cffffd200Name|r (type a new one), |cffffd200New profile|r, |cffffd200Copy profile|r and |cffffd200Delete profile|r. Delete asks first, takes every character's bindings in that profile with it, and moves its controllers to the first profile left. The last profile can't be deleted.", 2 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Controllers:|r every controller this computer knows and the profile it plays on.", 2 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Sync between machines:|r the switch, when it last synced and from where, what is on the server, |cffffd200Sync now|r and |cffffd200Undo last sync|r.", 2 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Backup:|r |cffffd200Export…|r and |cffffd200Import…|r.", 2 },
		{ "h", "Changed: Sync & backup moved to Settings" },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Triangle → More → Sync & backup|r and |cffffd200Tweaks → Controller → Sync between machines|r are gone: the switch, the status, Sync now, Undo, Export and Import are all in the Settings tab. /fct sync, /fct export and /fct import work as before.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Copy bindings from|r is gone too: Use or Copy a profile instead.", 1 },
		{ "b", "Profiles sync between your computers with everything else, and so does which profile each controller uses. Deleting a profile on one computer deletes it on the others.", 1 },
		{ "b", "An export holds this controller's profile (its name, layout and this character's bindings); an import goes into this controller's profile. Exports from 1.5.0 still import.", 1 },
		{ "b", "Sync from this version is written in a new format. A computer still on 1.5.0 pauses sync and says to update; it never writes over the newer copy. Update the addon on every computer you sync.", 1 },
	} },
	{ version = "1.5.0", date = "2026-11-21", blocks = {
		{ "h", "New: What's new" },
		{ "b", "After an update, a window shows once with what changed since the version you last saw: this list, newest first. It never opens in a fight or over another window, and a new install doesn't show it.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Never show again|r at its top right turns it off for good (it's never ticked for you). Type /fct whatsnew to see this version's notes and turn it back on.", 1 },
		{ "h", "New: a ring remembers your last pick" },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Middle|r, a new setting per ring in the Rings tab: |cffffd200Cancel|r (the default, as before) or |cffffd200Use last|r. With Use last, letting go of a Hold ring in the middle, or pressing |cffffd200Cross|r with nothing aimed, uses the slot you used last. Handy for totem and buff rings.", 1 },
		{ "b", "The buttons that open the ring (crossbar, Bindings, touch buttons) show that slot's icon, and so does the ring's middle while nothing is aimed.", 1 },
		{ "b", "Each character remembers its own last pick, across reloads. Change or empty that slot and it's forgotten.", 1 },
		{ "b", "Switch it from any button that opens the ring too: |cffffd200Triangle|r on the cell in Bindings (or on a touch button) shows |cffffd200Middle: Cancel|r / |cffffd200Middle: Use last|r. It's the ring's own setting, shared by every button that opens it.", 1 },
		{ "b", "A Toggle ring still opens on its button and closes on it again; |cffffd200Circle|r still cancels.", 1 },
		{ "h", "New: an arrow on ring buttons" },
		{ "b", "Every button that opens a ring has the game's small flyout arrow at its top edge, on the crossbar, in Bindings and on touch buttons, so you can tell them apart. Healer mode buttons keep their green cross instead.", 1 },
		{ "b", "The arrow hides while that ring is open, as the game's own flyout arrows do.", 1 },
		{ "b", "On by default. Turn it off with |cffffd200Arrow on ring buttons|r at the foot of the ring list in the Rings tab.", 1 },
		{ "h", "New: Healer mode remembers your last target" },
		{ "b", "In |cffffd200Bindings|r, on a button in Healer mode, |cffffd200Triangle|r shows |cffffd200Middle: Cancel|r under the Healer mode row. Pick it for |cffffd200Middle: Last target|r: letting go in the middle then casts on the place you last healed with that button, like Party 2.", 1 },
		{ "b", "While you hold the ring with the stick in the middle, that place lights up and shows its tooltip. If that unit can't be helped now (gone, hostile), nothing is cast.", 1 },
		{ "b", "It remembers the place, not the person, per button and per character. Off by default.", 1 },
		{ "h", "New: L3 and R3 in Bindings" },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200L3|r and |cffffd200R3|r (pressing a stick) have their own rows in Bindings, with a cell per bar, like a back paddle: put anything from the picker on L3 alone, on |cffffd200L2 + R3|r and so on. Rings opened from a stick press aim with the other stick when set to Dynamic.", 1 },
		{ "b", "A stick press is taken over only while one of its bars holds an action. Clear every bar and it's the game's again: |cffffd200L3|r auto-runs, |cffffd200R3|r pings. While one bar is used, the empty bars of that stick do nothing.", 1 },
		{ "b", "Until then its cells show what the game does with it, |cffffd200Auto-run|r or |cffffd200Ping|r, with the game's own icon, like the face buttons' Jump and Interact.", 1 },
		{ "h", "New: sort your bags with a stick press" },
		{ "b", "While your bags are open, |cffffd200L3|r sorts them. With the bags closed it works as usual (Auto-run). Not with a shoulder or trigger held.", 1 },
		{ "b", "The bags' controller footer shows it: an |cffffd200L3 Sort|r prompt joined to the end of Select · Collapse · Manage Bag · Close.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Tweaks → Bags & vendors → Sort bags key:|r L3 (the default), R3 or Off. This is the one tweak that starts on, so the Tweaks tab now says most are off until you turn them on.", 1 },
		{ "h", "New: your settings on every computer" },
		{ "b", "Play on a Mac and a handheld? Your bindings, rings, touch bars, controller setup, tweaks and keyboard settings (quick messages included) now follow you. The addon keeps a copy in a few account macros, |cffffd200FCT:Sync 1|r, |cffffd200FCT:Sync 2|r…, which the game stores for your account, and every computer you log in on uses the newest copy. On by default.", 1 },
		{ "b", "Each part goes on its own: change your rings on one computer and your tweaks on the other, and both arrive. When the same part changed on both, the newer one wins, chat says so, and |cffffd200Undo last sync|r brings yours back.", 1 },
		{ "b", "The first time on a computer that already has its own setup, it asks once: |cffffd200Use synced|r or |cffffd200Keep mine|r. Either way the other copy is kept for |cffffd200Undo last sync|r. A computer that hasn't read the synced copy yet never writes over it.", 1 },
		{ "b", "What stays on each computer: the keyboard's learned words, which slot a ring used last, Healer mode's last target, and the addon's own bookkeeping.", 1 },
		{ "b", "Bindings are kept per controller. A controller with no bindings yet offers |cffffd200Copy bindings from|r your other controller.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Triangle → More → Sync & backup|r on any tab shows when it last synced and from where, how many macros it uses and how many are free, and turns it off for this computer (the macros stay for the others). The same switch is in |cffffd200Tweaks → Controller → Sync between machines|r. /fct sync shows the same in chat; /fct sync now, on, off and undo do what they say.", 1 },
		{ "b", "The sync macros do nothing if pressed. Don't edit them in the Macros window; if one is changed or deleted, the addon writes them again. It never deletes a macro of yours, even one named FCT:Sync, and it never writes half a copy: when your account macros are full it says how many to free. /fct release deletes them too.", 1 },
		{ "h", "New: export and import" },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Sync & backup → Export…|r (or /fct export) shows your settings as text, already selected: Ctrl+C (Cmd+C on a Mac) copies it. It holds this character's bindings for this controller, touch bars, rings, tweaks, keyboard settings, options and the controller layout, and no character names, so you can share it.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Import…|r (or /fct import): paste with Ctrl+V (Cmd+V). It lists what would change, part by part; untick what you want to keep. Import asks once, and |cffffd200Undo last sync|r puts your old settings back. Pasting needs a keyboard.", 1 },
		{ "h", "Fixes" },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200No more piles of FCT: macros:|r the addon could lose track of one of its own macros (playing on a second computer, its settings reset, or a check at login that ran before the macro list had loaded) and then made \"FCT:Bags 2\", \"FCT:Bags 3\"… beside it, for game actions and other addons' buttons alike, filling the hidden action slots until touch buttons couldn't be added. It now recognises its own macros by name and text and reuses them, and a hidden slot that already holds the action a button wants (placed from your other computer) is reused instead of taking another. Once per login it also tidies what earlier versions left: one copy of each is kept, your buttons point at it, the extra copies are deleted and the hidden slots they held are freed. |cffffd200/fct cleanup|r does it on demand and says what it did. Your own macros are never touched, even one named FCT:.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Hidden action slots are shared between your computers and freed when no binding uses them.|r The addon now keeps a list of the hidden slots (keyboard bars 6-8) it placed on any of your computers, in the sync macros. A computer reuses a slot the other one placed for the same action, and frees one that no binding or touch button of that character uses any more, on any controller. Slots holding your own actions are never touched. Two buttons with the same action now share one hidden slot.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Touch buttons when every hidden slot is taken:|r adding an action no longer fails. It works right away as a macro, without a live cooldown or charges until a hidden slot frees up (its tooltip says so), then it gets one by itself.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Free up slots|r in the Touch tab: when your own actions sit on keyboard bars 6-8 (the hidden slots touch buttons and moved actions use), a button next to the slot counter lists them and, after you confirm, clears them from those bars. The spells, items and macros themselves stay.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Sort bags button:|r it could disappear behind the combined bags' title bar in the Gamepad UI. It now sits at the right end of the title bar and stays there.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Crossbar stuck after a held ring:|r with a modifier moved to another button (for example the right bar on L1), the crossbar could stay on that bar after a held ring or a heal, until you pressed the modifier again. It now always goes back.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Ring buttons showed an item count:|r a ring on a crossbar slot that held food or another stack showed that item's count on the ring's icon. The count is hidden now.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Aiming a heal with the left stick:|r after a held ring closes, the stick that aimed it stays held back while you cast or channel, so a heal aimed with the left stick isn't broken by walking. It's let go as soon as the stick is back in the middle, and a second after the cast ends at the latest.", 1 },
	} },
	{ version = "1.4.0", date = "2026-11-17", blocks = {
		{ "h", "New: Healer mode" },
		{ "p", "Any button that holds a heal can open a ring of your group: aim at someone and let go to cast on them." },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200On per button:|r focus a cell in Bindings (or a touch button in the Touch tab), press |cffffd200Triangle|r and pick |cffffd200Healer mode: On|r. Spells, spell groups and items can use it. A green cross marks the button in the windows and on your crossbar.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200The ring:|r the game's small round picker on the button you hold, with 7 places in fixed spots: You, Party 1 to 4, Target and Focus. Let go on someone to cast there, in the middle to cast nothing. Dead allies can be picked for a resurrection; a hostile target can't.", 1 },
		{ "b", "|cffffd200Each place|r shows the portrait, a health ring in the class colour, the role, incoming heals, shields, heal absorbs, a red pulse under 30% health, and a debuff you can dispel. The person you aim at gets the game's own tooltip.", 1 },
		{ "b", "Works on face buttons, the D-pad, paddles, crossbar slots and touch buttons, in combat too. No settings: it always shows while held and aims with the stick for that button.", 1 },
	} },
}
